## 2. Tic sweep: 17 instances of rule 12

Headings first, since the rule says the shape is worst there. Notable: `## The deliverable already exists, and a ministry has already published it` → `## A ministry has already published this deliverable` (the style guide's own example), and `## The equation needs three numbers, and the tool exists to build them` → `## The base machine, before any climate`. Also "Climate scenarios lower growth, and that is the only way climate enters the equation" → "Lowering growth is the only way climate enters the equation"; "The second claim is narrower than the first, and the difference matters" → single clause. The other 318 occurrences of ", and" join two different facts; nine headings I deliberately kept are listed with reasons so the judgment is auditable.

